# Line endings are LF everywhere, including on Windows checkouts.
#
# This is not a style preference. `crates/cluster/tests/golden/` holds
# byte-exact expectations for the YAML writer, compared against what the
# renderer produces — and the renderer emits `\n` on every platform. Git for
# Windows converts text files to CRLF on checkout by default, so those fixtures
# arrived with `\r\n` and every golden test failed with an "expected" and a
# "rendered" block that were identical to look at.
#
# Normalising in the test would have hidden the difference instead of fixing it,
# and would have hidden a real stray `\r` in the output along with it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: no line-ending conversion, no diffing as text.
*.png binary
*.icns binary
*.dmg binary
*.p12 binary
*.p8 binary
